 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** $O(R^3)$ for cube iteration, with hash map operations assumed $O(1)$ on average. Total vertices $N \le 8 R^3$.
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(R^3)$ for cubes, $O(N)$ for vertices.
-- **Performance:** Not given in the sources.
-- **Strengths:** Reduces vertex count by deduplicating shared corners, ensuring consistent topology.
-- **Limitations:** Hash map overhead may be significant for very high resolutions.
-- **When to use:** When constructing a voxel grid for subsequent mesh extraction (e.g., FlexiCubes) where shared vertices are required.
-- **When not to use:** When a simple, non-deduplicated grid is sufficient or when memory is extremely constrained and hash map overhead is prohibitive.
